!Engagement samples

Support engineering is distinguished by its proximity to the user, bringing with it the satisfaction of affecting a customer’s long-term success via the adoption of a new technology or product.

This means more than simply helping customers when the product isn’t working: support engagements can involve 

* pre-deployment planning
* onboarding with customers
* working with customers to get necessary documentation and training
* and then helping customers rapidly resolve issues at critical times – wherever those issues may lie.

As with many aspects of engineering, this includes attending to unseen (and under appreciated!) details; please describe <span style="color: #db89c8;">at least two examples</span> of customer support engagements you have led, or in which you were otherwise deeply involved. 
